---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
// TODO before merge (operator decision): the founder is currently unnamed on this page.
// Decide which public name (and optionally email) to publish, then fill in the
// "Who Runs This" section. Anonymity + service business is a hard sell; a named
// operator with modest claims is the strongest configuration.
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Cascadia Mobile Research — an independent field-data and spatial computing lab in Portland, Oregon"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">About</h1>
        <div class="mb-8 border-l-4 border-accent-blue bg-dark-surface/50 p-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-text-primary">
            <strong>Cascadia Mobile Research LLC is an independent lab in Portland, Oregon that
            pairs field data collection — drones, LiDAR, and sensors — with spatial data processing
            on infrastructure it owns and operates.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Statement -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <p>
          The premise is simple: the interesting problems in small-scale geospatial work live in
          the whole pipeline, not just the aircraft. Anyone can buy a drone. Producing a
          measurement someone can rely on — knowing its accuracy, documenting its provenance,
          processing it without shipping the data to a third party — takes instruments, compute,
          and method working together. That combination is what this lab builds.
        </p>
        <p>
          The structure is deliberate: client services and open research under one roof. Services
          keep the lab honest about what actually matters in the field and fund the equipment and
          time that research requires. Research keeps the services honest — every capability we
          sell is one we've tested and written up. Neither side is decoration for the other.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Operator -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            The lab is run by one engineer, with a background in data systems and graduate
            training in geography and spatial analysis. The person who scopes your project is
            the one who flies it, processes it, and stands behind the numbers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Principles -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Principles</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-text-secondary">
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">
              Empirical Grounding
            </h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Claims are backed by measurement. Methods are evaluated on real hardware and real
              sites, and accuracy limits are stated rather than implied. Hypotheses are tested,
              not assumed.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">
              Open Methods
            </h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Experiments, benchmarks, and methodology are published in the open — including
              failures and negative results. Clients can read the testing behind the services;
              other practitioners can check the work.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">
              Data Sovereignty
            </h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Processing runs on infrastructure the lab owns. Client data does not pass through
              third-party cloud platforms, and the full chain from capture to deliverable can be
              documented.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-text-primary">
              Long-Term Orientation
            </h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              The lab is built for sustained work over years: instruments that are maintained,
              documentation that serves as institutional memory, and a notebook that compounds
              rather than resets.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What This Is / Is Not -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">What This Is — and Isn't</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-text-primary">This is a working business.</strong> Cascadia Mobile
            Research LLC is a registered Oregon company that takes on client work. Revenue funds
            the instruments, the infrastructure, and the research time.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-text-primary">This is also a real lab.</strong> The open notebook
            isn't marketing garnish — experiments are run and documented to the standards described
            in the <a href="/research" class="link">lab notes</a>, whether or not a client is
            paying for them.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-text-primary">This is not a venture-backed startup.</strong> There
            is no growth-at-all-costs trajectory and no investor deck. The goal is a durable,
            competent practice that compounds slowly.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-text-primary">This is not a cloud service.</strong> All processing
            runs on self-hosted, physical infrastructure — a choice made for data governance,
            cost control, and the ability to understand our own pipeline end to end.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          A dedicated contact page is on its way. Until then, the best way to reach the lab is
          through GitHub.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/cascadia-systems-lab"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a href="/services" class="btn btn-secondary">
            View Services
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
